From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000055 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Petr Parkan Janda <petronijus@bastla.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: OMAP4: pm: steelhead: stock's boot PM setup for deep idle

What stock 3.0.8 set up before its deep C-states ran, and mainline does not
(stock-parity audit of reverse-eng/vmlinux.bin, 2026-09-23):

 - MPU and CORE rest at ON (stock pwrdms_setup, 0xc0012d04); cpuidle
   programs them per entry and puts them back. Mainline's pwrdms_setup()
   arms both for RET, CORE with logic OFF, permanently -- so a CORE that
   ever idled would drop into OSWR without any context save. Live on r14:
   PM_CORE_PWRSTCTRL 0x03ff0f01.
 - PRM_PWRREQCTRL = 3 and PRM_CLKREQCTRL = 2 (0xc0013150, 0xc0013048);
   mainline leaves both at 0. TWL6030 sleep, and with it the TPS62361
   VDD_MPU enable (SYSEN in the APE group, patch 0014), follows PWRREQ, so
   it must not drop while the MPU holds retained state. Latent until CORE
   retains, but required before it does.
 - DISABLE_RTA_EXPORT in PRM_SRAM_WKUP_SETUP and PRM_LDO_SRAM_{CORE,MPU,
   IVA}_SETUP (0xc0012f64-0xc0012fd0, every OMAP4). The ROM already leaves
   them set on this unit; do not depend on it.

Not done here, deliberately: clearing PRM_VOLTCTRL's AUTO_CTRL fields.
With the VDD_*_I2C_DISABLE bits mainline sets, AUTO_CTRL sends no
retention-voltage command at all (VDD_MPU stays at the OPP voltage through
retention), and stock's table no longer retains the MPU in C2. Aligning
the VC policy with stock belongs with any change that enables RET voltage.

Also note: the MPU/CORE ON written here does not survive boot on its own --
the PRM genpd driver re-arms both for RET at late_initcall_sync. The
steelhead DTS patch 0057 takes those two domains out of genpd.

Signed-off-by: Petr Parkan Janda <petronijus@bastla.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-omap2/pm44xx.c b/arch/arm/mach-omap2/pm44xx.c
index 37b1681..aa96354 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-omap2/pm44xx.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-omap2/pm44xx.c
@@ -15,11 +15,16 @@
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <asm/system_misc.h>
 
+#include <linux/of.h>
+
 #include "soc.h"
 #include "common.h"
 #include "clockdomain.h"
 #include "powerdomain.h"
 #include "pm.h"
+#include "prcm44xx.h"
+#include "prm44xx.h"
+#include "prminst44xx.h"
 
 u16 pm44xx_errata;
 
@@ -147,6 +152,66 @@ static int __init pwrdms_setup(struct powerdomain *pwrdm, void *unused)
 	return omap_set_pwrdm_state(pwrst->pwrdm, pwrst->next_state);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Nexus Q (OMAP4460 HS): what stock set up before its deep C-states ran, and
+ * mainline does not. Offsets in PRM_DEVICE (the 6.18 headers stop at 0xac).
+ */
+#define STEELHEAD_PRM_CLKREQCTRL		0x000c
+#define STEELHEAD_PRM_PWRREQCTRL		0x0014
+#define STEELHEAD_PRM_SRAM_WKUP_SETUP		0x00b4
+#define STEELHEAD_PRM_LDO_SRAM_CORE_SETUP	0x00b8
+#define STEELHEAD_PRM_LDO_SRAM_MPU_SETUP	0x00c0
+#define STEELHEAD_PRM_LDO_SRAM_IVA_SETUP	0x00c8
+#define STEELHEAD_DISABLE_RTA_EXPORT		BIT(0)
+
+static void __init omap4_steelhead_pm_setup(void)
+{
+	static const u16 rta[] __initconst = {
+		STEELHEAD_PRM_SRAM_WKUP_SETUP, STEELHEAD_PRM_LDO_SRAM_CORE_SETUP,
+		STEELHEAD_PRM_LDO_SRAM_MPU_SETUP, STEELHEAD_PRM_LDO_SRAM_IVA_SETUP,
+	};
+	struct powerdomain *pd;
+	int i;
+
+	/*
+	 * MPU and CORE rest at ON (stock pwrdms_setup, 0xc0012d04); cpuidle
+	 * programs them per deep entry and puts them back afterwards. The
+	 * generic setup above armed both for RET -- CORE with logic OFF -- for
+	 * good, which a CORE that ever idled would have entered without any
+	 * context save.
+	 */
+	pd = pwrdm_lookup("mpu_pwrdm");
+	if (pd)
+		omap_set_pwrdm_state(pd, PWRDM_POWER_ON);
+	pd = pwrdm_lookup("core_pwrdm");
+	if (pd)
+		omap_set_pwrdm_state(pd, PWRDM_POWER_ON);
+
+	/*
+	 * PWRREQ released only when every domain is OFF, CLKREQ condition 2 --
+	 * stock's values (0xc0013150, 0xc0013048). TWL6030 sleep, and with it
+	 * the TPS62361 VDD_MPU enable, follows PWRREQ, so it must never drop
+	 * while the MPU holds retained state. Only relevant once CORE retains.
+	 */
+	omap4_prminst_write_inst_reg(0x3, OMAP4430_PRM_PARTITION,
+				     OMAP4430_PRM_DEVICE_INST,
+				     STEELHEAD_PRM_PWRREQCTRL);
+	omap4_prminst_write_inst_reg(0x2, OMAP4430_PRM_PARTITION,
+				     OMAP4430_PRM_DEVICE_INST,
+				     STEELHEAD_PRM_CLKREQCTRL);
+
+	/*
+	 * Retention-till-access off for the SRAM wake-up and the CORE/MPU/IVA
+	 * SRAM LDOs, as stock set on every OMAP4 (0xc0012f64-0xc0012fd0). The
+	 * ROM leaves them set on this unit already; do not depend on that.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(rta); i++)
+		omap4_prminst_rmw_inst_reg_bits(STEELHEAD_DISABLE_RTA_EXPORT,
+						STEELHEAD_DISABLE_RTA_EXPORT,
+						OMAP4430_PRM_PARTITION,
+						OMAP4430_PRM_DEVICE_INST, rta[i]);
+}
+
 /**
  * omap_default_idle - OMAP4 default ilde routine.'
  *
@@ -265,6 +330,9 @@ int __init omap4_pm_init(void)
 		goto err2;
 	}
 
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("google,steelhead"))
+		omap4_steelhead_pm_setup();
+
 	if (cpu_is_omap44xx())
 		ret = omap4plus_init_static_deps(omap4_static_dep_map);
 	else if (soc_is_omap54xx() || soc_is_dra7xx())
